# Personal data backed up by the `vault-backup` job, as plain hardlinked snapshots under
# a local directory. Not encrypted: Timeshift already keeps these same files unencrypted
# on the same disk, so a second encrypted copy protected nothing and only added a key to lose.
# This list is deliberately explicit and version-controlled: it is the answer to
# "what does your backup contain?". Work repositories are NOT here by design --
# company and system data are covered by Timeshift, separately.
# Lines are paths; ~/ is expanded; missing paths are skipped and counted.

~/powerhouse                      # Obsidian vault: health, meds, salah, daily notes
~/.local/share/timetrack          # work.db + private.db (own time records)
~/.local/share/adhd               # salah log
~/.local/share/timewarrior        # human work intervals
~/.task                           # taskwarrior: tickets + AI-generated subtasks
~/.config/timetrack               # payroll + holiday policy (unmanaged, sensitive)
~/.config/adhd                    # prayer + iqamah times
